    "poster_id": 652,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > be the largest subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/527e4f071ba18c0a327840643c7daf1731d0b7d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" > such that for each <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/6550276377d461aa90435ac0d2f08dfbef079a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > divides at most one other element in <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" >.</span> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab163d0f6e7854ab0e705e49c9a2a9d81db3c3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2n}3\\leq |A|\\leq \\left\\lceil \\frac{3n}4\\right\\rceil. \\]\"  width=\"145\" height=\"43\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $A$ be the largest subset of $\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$ such that for each $x\\in A$, $x$ divides at most one other element in $A$. Prove that \\[\\frac{2n}3\\leq |A|\\leq \\left\\lceil \\frac{3n}4\\right\\rceil. \\]",
