    "poster_id": 167643,
    "post_rendered": "<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" > is a point inside triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/2844f24a6b72846f9ff5a333c7d3d8e748b76b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA=OB+OC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" >.</span> Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a1063394bdae0204b66338ce14b712e8dbf6e645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#039;,C&#039;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"19\" > be midpoints of arcs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0129518bfc1d0df50eeb37d3d6a62b0a0327a85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd97737c9a1eb5146725902d4e4c4bda1388129b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOB$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" >.</span> Prove that circumcircles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9eec0a0e8d02b6ae913cb6198ef16e3e2e8a1b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COC&#039;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0ccb52492eb0df03677e0fe8c4737389c591ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOB&#039;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" > are tangent to each other.<br>\n<br>\n<span class=\"cmty-hide-heading faux-link\" onclick=\"AoPS.Community.Utils.clickHide($(this));\" href=\"#\">Click to reveal hidden text</span><div class=\"cmty-hide-content\" style=\"display:none\">wording fixed</div>",
    "post_canonical": "$O$ is a point inside triangle $ABC$ such that $OA=OB+OC$. Suppose $B',C'$ be midpoints of arcs $AOC$ and $AOB$. Prove that circumcircles $COC'$ and $BOB'$ are tangent to each other.\n\n[hide]wording fixed[/hide]",
